layout: index
headline: Moleculer
description: Moleculer is a microservices framework for Node.js and TypeScript with built-in service discovery, load balancing, circuit breakers, distributed tracing and an event bus — no Kubernetes, Consul or service mesh required.
subtitle: Microservices framework for Node.js and TypeScript.
tagline: Service discovery, load balancing, circuit breakers, distributed tracing and a built-in event bus — without Kubernetes, Consul, Istio or a service mesh. Start as a modular monolith, split into distributed services later without changing your code.
comments: false
---
ul#intro-feature-list
    li.intro-feature-wrap
        .intro-feature
            .intro-feature-icon
                i.fa.fa-server
            h3.intro-feature-title No infrastructure to run
            p.intro-feature-desc
                | Service registry, service discovery, load balancing and health checks are built into the framework — not into Consul, etcd or a Kubernetes control plane.
                a(href='/docs/0.15/registry.html') Read about discovery.
    li.intro-feature-wrap
        .intro-feature
            .intro-feature-icon
                i.fa.fa-heartbeat
            h3.intro-feature-title Resilient by default
            p.intro-feature-desc
                | Circuit breaker, bulkhead, retry, timeout and fallback are part of the framework, not bolted on with extra libraries.
                a(href='/docs/0.15/fault-tolerance.html') See fault tolerance.
    li.intro-feature-wrap
        .intro-feature
            .intro-feature-icon
                i.fa.fa-exchange-alt
            h3.intro-feature-title Pluggable transport
            p.intro-feature-desc
                | The same service code runs over TCP, NATS, Redis, Kafka, MQTT or AMQP. Swap the message broker without touching a service.
                a(href='/docs/0.15/networking.html') Compare transporters.
    li.intro-feature-wrap
        .intro-feature
            .intro-feature-icon
                i.fa.fa-chart-line
            h3.intro-feature-title Observable
            p.intro-feature-desc
                | Built-in metrics (Prometheus, StatsD, Datadog) and distributed tracing (Jaeger, Zipkin, Datadog, New Relic) — no sidecar, no agent.
                a(href='/docs/0.15/tracing.html') Learn about tracing.
    li.intro-feature-wrap
        .intro-feature
            .intro-feature-icon
                i.fa.fa-bolt
            h3.intro-feature-title Blazing fast
            p.intro-feature-desc
                | High-performance microservices framework. Check the
                a(href='/docs/benchmark.html') benchmark results!
    li.intro-feature-wrap
        .intro-feature
            .intro-feature-icon
                i.fa.fa-code
            h3.intro-feature-title Open source
            p.intro-feature-desc
                | Moleculer is a 100% open source and free of charge project. All source code is available under the MIT License on GitHub. All built-in modules (caching, serializer, transporter) are pluggable —
                a(href='/modules.html') find all modules.
